ink?\par \par \uc2 WILLIAMS: Well, you know, look, I think there's history here. I mean, alcohol has always been a social lubricant for people. And I think part of it -- I remember college days, people would say hey, you know, I'm going to get a shot of courage before I go talk to that girl. And I mean shot of courage was, you know, a shot of tequila or something. OK.\par \par \uc2 But you know there's a great danger in there, I think. I just think it unleashes a lot attitudes that maybe aren't good and I just can't recommend it. I don't think it's a good move.\par \par \uc2 PAVLICH: All right, "ONE MORE THING" up next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)'\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: All right, time for "ONE MORE THING." I'll go first.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Greg's sports corner.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: You heard that whistle, right? Only humans can be refs. But will that remain in the future as we get more involved in -- what am I saying? Let's look at this dog who wants to be a ref.\par \par \uc2 I love this dog. Oh my God. Oh, my God. He's the greatest. That, Jesse, is a Dachshund, I believe.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Oh, I was going to say Wiener dog.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: It's not a Dachshund?\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: I don't know. Who cares?\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Isn't that the same thing?\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Jesse, you just like to say Wiener. You're disgusting. All right, Juan.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: That's like Netherland in Holland.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Yes. You're up, Juan.\par \par \uc2 WILLIAMS: That sound -- it sounded -- it remind me of that shower scene in psycho, that shrieking sound.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: It's true.\par \par \uc2 WILLIAMS: Anyway, time for tonight's weather report, folks. And it comes straight from a carnival funhouse mirror. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: It's the current temperature righ