od, if they're restaurants, they're paying more for energy if you're a bakery, you use a lot of energy.\par \par \uc2 So, all of these problems seem beyond the capacity of these bureaucrats. They're trying to manage a multi trillion-dollar system and it doesn't work in real world as it does in the classroom or in bureaucrats mind.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Yes, then we cancelled the Keystone Pipeline. Now you've got a pipeline that's having problem, you know, off of -- across the third, 19 states of the country. Why do you have eggs?\par \par \uc2 ASMAN: Because our stage manager has duck eggs and they sell for -- you can still -- if you -- you know, this is one thing, you can go to local farmers and I think you're going to see a lot more of this, people are pinching pennies. These cost me $3.00 for a dozen, which is a great deal and they're terrific duck eggs.\par \par \uc2 But I think people are going to start avoiding looking for alternatives than the supermarkets and go directly to farmers in order to get the best deals because the prices are through the roof.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: They're 22.50 around the corner. I don't know why --\par \par \uc2 ASMAN: I think I got a good deal from Brian (PH).\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: (INAUDIBLE) I want to -- I want to get some duck eggs. Thank you. Thank you, David.\par \par \uc2 ASMAN: Of course, my pleasure.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Good to see you as always.\par \par \uc2 So, at this hour, switching gears here, police are on a manhunt for this individual suspected of opening fire about a block and a half from here in New York City.\par \par \uc2 A 4 year old girl was caught in the crossfire Geraldo Rivera and Tomi Lahren are here on the alarming uptick in crime in our cities across the country.\par \par \uc2 And still ahead, my exclusive interview with \uc2 Randi Weingarten\uc2 , head of the AFT on whether the unions have undue influence over the White House.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Bre