hrough right now.\par \par \uc2 HOGAN: Police releasing this new body camera footage of officer Alyssa Vogel running for medical help after securing a tourniquet on the child. Something she's never had to do in her time as an officer.\par \par \uc2 Two others were shot in Times Square, among them a 43 year old woman and a 23 year old woman visiting New York from her -- with her family. And this is what she had to say.\par \par \uc2 WENDY MAGRINAT, WOUNDED: I felt it in my leg. And but there was more shots and my main concern was to get my daughter to safety.\par \par \uc2 HOGAN: Right.\par \par \uc2 MAGRINAT: So, I didn't tell anyone at the moment. I just held my hand where the hole was.\par \par \uc2 HOGAN: Police are still searching for 31 year old Farah Khan Muhammad and he was identified by his brother who says that he was the intended victim.\par \par \uc2 Last year, police charged him with another random assault for allegedly hitting another man.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HOGAN (on camera): Now, we have seen a large increase in gun violence here in New York City. Just last month alone, shootings increased by 166 percent compared to April of last year. And within just this weekend, we've seen 20 people shot in the city of course, including the three who were shot here in Times Square, Martha.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: What a mess. Alex, thank you very much. Fox News correspondent- at-large Geraldo Rivera, and Fox nation host Tomi Lahren join me now. Good to have both of you with us.\par \par \uc2 GERALDO RIVERA, FOX NEWS CORRESPONDENT-AT-LARGE: Thanks, Martha, hi.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: You know, I just want to go back and play this. This is soundbite from Bill de Blasio the mayor on June 23rd, 2020. Listen to this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BILL DE BLASIO (D), MAYOR OF NEW YORK: So, it proves the change can come. But we need a lot more change.\par \par \uc2 So, one of the things we're going to be working on going forward is making sure there's a much better mechanism for weeding out the cops who should not be on the force.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: So, now here we are. You've heard about how much with these shootings have escalated. I haven't seen the city this dangerous in decades, decades, Geraldo.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: You know, Martha, he wants a mechanism by which we can weed out bad cops. We need a mechanism by which we can weed out bad people.\par \par \uc2 Murder is out 36 percent in the New York City, this is the worst mayor ever. Three were shot dead. Harlem, South Bronx over the weekend. You know, the two women and the 4 year old toddler. I'm so glad that they're all going to be OK and thank God for the heroic cop.\par \par \uc2 But there, they get a lot of attention because they're tourists in Times Square of all places, a block from the headquarters of Fox News.\par \par \uc2 But the mayhem that's out there, there were nine mass shootings in the country this weekend. Nine mass shootings which four more victims this weekend, big cities, Martha, must consider reinstituting stop and frisk. It works to reduce gun violence. We have to implement it in a fair colorblind manner.\par \par \uc2 Gun control crews could implement techniques similar to what the TSA uses or DUI stops. We've got to do something despite bail reform. We must insist on high bail for gun crimes, Martha.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Andrew Cuomo said it's not the OK Corral in New York City. It sure do look like it yesterday, Tomi?\par \par \uc2 TOMI LAHREN, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Yes, I think we also need to take a step back and look beyond just New York City. But all of these Democrat-run cities that have diverted money away from their police departments that have placated to groups like BLM who have demonized police officers and also have encouraged lawlessness.\par \par \uc2 I mean, we see lawlessness at our southern border. We see lawlessness in our cities. We see groups of people who feel now emboldened if they're angry about something that they can loot the target of the \uc2 Foot Locker\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And you see places like New York City, again, run by Democrats and I'm glad that Geraldo did call out the mayor there, but it's bigger than this.\par \par \uc2 You've got these bail reform, cashless bail, which is essentially catch and release, you've got other felon coddling policies that are impacting mostly Democrat-run cities and states.\par \par \uc2 But then, you've got a nationwide narrative under the BLM umbrella that is not only demonizing police, but also glorifying lawlessness, resisting arrest.\par \par \uc2 And I also want to go back to this talk about gun control, because a lot of folks are really turning to that now saying we've got a spike in gun crimes, that might be true. But the solution for these Democrats who want to defund police departments is always to go after the rights of law abiding Americans, they create a problem and their solution to that problem is bigger government and infringing upon our rights even more than they already have.\par \par \uc2 Excuse me, that's not the problem. We don't have a gun problem, we have a thug problem. And these Democrats need a day of reckoning to understand that.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Yes, well, just take a walk down the streets in New York. I got to leave it there, guys. Thank you very much. It is absolutely a disaster safety needs to return to this city and all cities across this country and it takes leadership at the top to make it happen.\par \par \uc2 We know what it's like, we know what it looks like under Bloomberg. We know what it looks like under Giuliani and somebody's got to figure it out here and all across this great country.\par \par \uc2 Tomi and Geraldo, thank you. Great to have you both here.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: Thank you, Martha.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Thanks, you guys.\par \par \uc2 So, coming up. You don't want to miss this; \uc2 Randi Weingart