hannon Bream, Jesses Watters, Jeanine Pirro,  Lawrence Jones \par \uc2 7,767 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 May 2021\par \uc2 Fox News: The Five\par \uc2 FOXFIV\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2021 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2021 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 NEIL CAVUTO, FOX NEWS ANCHOR: But the fact to the matter is, it is a very, very big worry. We will be chronicling that. But again, I want to advise that things could be worse because we're also monitoring something else that rocket that is hurdling to earth which if it obliterates a good chunk of earth all of this stuff passes, right? We'll see you tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 JUAN WILLIAMS, FOX NEWS HOST: Hello, everyone. I'm Juan Williams, along with Shannon Bream, Jesses Watters, Judge Jeanine Pirro and Lawrence Jones. It's five o'clock in New York City. And this is The Five.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: One size does not fit all and adults who have higher risk should not expect the youth to carry the burden of those fears.\par \par \uc2 (CROWD CHEERING)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: You will listen to us.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Nope, we've had our citizen participation. All right.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Let us speak.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: No more masks! No more masks! No more masks!\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: I move that we adjourn this meeting.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Five seconds.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: You will listen to us.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Nope, we've had our citizen participation.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 WILLIAMS: A major battle over COVID restrictions breaking out in America even as cases drop. Frustrated parents protesting mask mandates for kids during a wide school meeting in Utah. Things got heated after parents were told their children will still need to wear mask until the end of the school year.\par \par \uc2 Police are reportedly investigating some of those protesting for disrupting the public proceedings. The K through 12 mask mandate is a state health order and school districts in Utah do not -- do not have the authority to overturn it. Utah's governor now says the state will not mandate masks for students in the fall.\par \par \uc2 Our Fox News medical experts say the parents have a point on lifting the restrictions.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MARC SIEGEL, FOX NEWS MEDICAL CORRESPONDENT: What are they talking about mandating that children wear masks in schools still when children are not the spreaders of this, children are not getting sick from this usually. From a public health point of view, I don't believe the mandate is necessary.\par \par \uc2 NICOLE SAPHIER, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: The CDC is the only entity recommending two years and up to wear face mask. The \uc2 World Health Organization\uc2  doesn't even recommend younger children wear them and they say the five -- the 12-year-olds should really be on a case-by-case basis because there is risk versus benefit with it.\par \par \uc2 So, the mask -- the science with mask wearing in young children is not as black-and-white as the CDC would like you to think.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 WILLIAMS: And President Biden being grilled on why he stills wear -- he is still wearing a mask.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: Because I'm worried about you. No, it's a joke. It's a joke. Why am I wearing the mask? Because when we're inside it is still good policy to wear the mask, that's why. When I'm outside, and the problem is lots of times I walk away from this podium you notice I forget to put my mask back on because I'm used to not wearing it outside.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 WILLIAMS: Jesse, I was just thinking, I think we all get the parents frustration here, but I'm just thinking to myself, the CDC, the state government, are they simply being conservative with schoolchildren despite the drop in the rate of infections?\par \par \uc2 JESSE WATTERS, FOX NEWS HOST: Well, first of all, let's hear it for Utah coming out of nowhere to lead The Five on a Friday. I did not see that coming, real Cinderella story of all the 50 states. Good for Utah.\par \par \uc2 Yes. Parents going wild, it's always fun to watch although they should probably behave a little bit better. But you know better than anybody, Juan. When moms are getting mad like this, you know something is seriously wrong, and that's what I'm saying.\par \par \uc2 You -- they are angry out of love because they don't want their child being slapped with a mask five days a week for a year, the science has says it's not necessary and if you just take Utah out of all the 50 states, the pandemic barely penetrated there.\par \par \uc2 They only lost 2,000 people in Utah compared to 50,000 in New York. It wasn't even the leading cause of death. I think it was 11th of all the reasons people died last year in the state of Utah. The population density in Utah, you need binoculars to see your neighbor. It's a very healthy state. It is not spreading in that state at all.\par \par \uc2 I think the numbers show right now nearly all of the elderly in Utah are vaccinated, about half of the adult population parents can get the shot, teachers can get that shot, we're fine in Utah. They're like this close to coming out of the pandemic. And the fact that police would think about pressing charges --\par \par \uc2 LAWRENCE JONES, FOX NEWS HOST: Bingo.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: -- did you see a crime? I didn't see a crime. I saw a bunch of yelling. If yelling is a crime then Judge Jeanine should be doing 25 to life.\