rty is going to be popping. I'm going to have whiskey, fireworks, a newborn baby. What could possibly go wrong?\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Exactly.\par \par \uc2 MCDOWELL: Amen. \uc2 Liberty\uc2 , freedom. Hot freedom! By the way, I haven't been vaccinated because I had COVID and so I have antibodies. I will be getting vaccinated and it's not political. I tell everybody to do it. So, (inaudible).\par \par \uc2 Coming up, the revolt against woke schools in America, parents and teachers fighting back against liberal indoctrination.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Well, it seems like it's a revolt that is starting to gain a little bit of traction now about the inundation of woke teaching in nearly every aspect of many American schools today. Parents are now suing the Biden administration because they are pushing critical race theory by making it a criteria for schools who want to receive grants. It all goes back to the money. So, the National Review pinpoints where the problem began saying that we're seeing -- what we're seeing now began, as many of us has talked about for years, on college campuses.\par \par \uc2 And just this week, the head of an elite New York City private school was recorded -- admitting basically. He said that it goes too far, but he hasn't done anything about it. Listen.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PAUL ROSSI, MATH TEACHER, GRACE CHURCH SCHOOL: So, you agree that you were demonizing kids?\par \par \uc2 GEORGE DAVISON PRINCIPAL GRACE CHURCH SCHOOL: We're demonizing kids. We're demonizing white people, for being born.\par \par \uc2 ROSSI: \uc2 OK, so, we're demonizing white -- we're demonizing white kids. Why don't you just say it?\par \par \uc2 DAVISON: We are -- we are using language that makes them feel less than, for nothing that they are personally responsible for.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: So, this is the head of the school. He's admitting that he knows that there's something innately wrong with what they're doing, and yet he shows no sign -- in fact, he fire -- they essentially fired -- he's not allowed to teach anymore, has been pushed out of the classroom.\par \par \uc2 So, Jesse if they know it, and he understands that it's an issue, why don't they -- why is no reluctance to change?\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: And he's afraid of the mob. And the mob is a minority, but he's still terrified. I want everybody in the audience to think back about how they were in high school. You're sexually active, you're starting to drive, you're experimenting with things. You're doing sports, you're doing extracurriculars, you're arguing with your mom and your dad.\par \par \uc2 There's fights in school, there's social drama, you can barely keep your head on straight. You're too fat, you're too skinny, your skin is breaking out. With all that chaos and tenderness and insecurity. You're going to now take a white student and jam an hour a day of telling him you have to be ashamed of yourself, your father, your grandfather, your great grandfather, you are racist inherently, and you are succeeding because of white supremacy, and patriarchy.\par \par \uc2 And then, you go to the Black student and you say you're a victim, you're always going to be a victim. Everybody that looks at you only sees your skin color. And the White kid you sit across from in chemistry class is continuing to suppress you through microaggressions.\par \par \uc2 What kind of monster would do that to a student? I'll tell you what, Martha, a Marxist, because that's where this comes from. Think about it. We're competing against the world. The rest of the world is learning Mandarin, Chinese, computer science. They're reading the classics. And we're teaching our students to hate themselves.\par \par \uc2 That just divides us. It makes us angry. It makes us not as smart and less competitive. And that's what this is all about. It's like the enemy within, psychological warfare.\par \par \uc2 M