s to be true -- and I don`t know if it is, that`s why I think investigations have to happen, you have to allow them to play out -- then I think Governor Cuomo will find himself in a different set of trouble if the nursing home crisis data that he reported is not true.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: Byron, the Cuomo administration`s response, "The out of facility data was omitted after DOH," their Department of Health, "could not confirm it had been adequately verified. It did not change the conclusion of the report." Byron?\par \par \uc2 YORK: I don`t think anybody`s really going to accept that. I think the developments today were actually pretty good in the sense that they refocused attention on to the nursing home problem and what the governor did and the life-and-death issue of COVID, away from his Me Too issues, which still may be the greater threat for him staying in office.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: And Mollie, what about that, because it seems like people have been beating the drum about these thousands of elderly people who were basically the most vulnerable and died, and yet it was the Me Too allegations that seem to have him in real hot water?\par \par \uc2 HEMINGWAY: Everything is interesting because a year ago we were told this governor was doing the best in the entire country when in fact everything we were told about his performance was a lie. This policy was wrong, this policy of sending people who were sick into the nursing homes, precisely the opposite thing than what should have been done. Then the cover up. I don`t know if these are criminal, but they are extremely serious. The treatment of women in his midst is also a problem for him, but in terms of public policy and of the ramifications of what he did with his handling of COVID, it is appalling what we were told versus what the reality is.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: OK, Mollie, stay with you, we will do a lightning round on the economy. Today the February jobs numbers, 379,000 jobs added, that`s the most since October, 6.2 unemployment rate, it was down. Quick round-robin on this. We`ll start with you on this, Mollie.\par \par \uc2 HEMINGWAY: These are good numbers, but these are -- the problem is that we have to have much stronger numbers, and we have a president right now who his first actions were about killing jobs. He`s talking about regulating things. That removal of regulations did so much to help the economy prior to the coronavirus, so we will have to see how things go in the long run.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: And Byron, some Republicans are arguing that these bright spots mean we don`t necessarily need a $2 trillion recovery package. They`re going to use it for that argument.\par \par \uc2 YORK: There you go. It has put the White House and Democrats in kind of an odd situation of needing to talk down the economy to emphasize how desperately needed immediate passage of this $1.9 trillion bill is. It`s a little bit of a conflict going on there.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: Harold, your take on the numbers and how they play on Capitol Hill?\par \par \uc2 FORD: I love great numbers. I don`t care if it comes from a Republican or a Democrat president. But the market is always six months ahead of Main Street. Help Main Street get to where the markets are and Wall Street might be. The reports came out that rich people did better during COVID. Let`s help Main Street catch up. Pass the COVID relief package.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: OK, we`ve got a little bit of time now to work through Winners and Losers. So Harold, I will start with you.\par \par \uc2 FORD: My winner is Colonel Anthony Henderson. He`s going to be promoted to Brigadier General. No black American has ever been a four-star officer in the Marines. I hope he gets there.\par \par \uc2 My loser is our culture. This cancel culture stuff has to stop. Dr. Seuss was really another icing on the cake for me. He was no racist. He may have been a little uninformed, but our country is better than this. We shouldn`t reduce Dr. Seuss to the Salem witch trial. Come on America, come on politicians, come on politics, be better than this.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: Harold, do you worry about banning, essentially the modern-day equivalent of burning them, if you can`t get them on the open market?\par \par \uc2 FORD: Some books may deserve to be burned, ones that I got D`s and F`s on in high schools, but definitely, definitely not Dr. Seuss.\par \par \uc2 SANDERS: OK, Byron, to you, winners and losers?\par \par \uc2 YORK: My winner are the Americans who are hoping to get in the COVID vaccine. This week the average of doses administered hit 2 million per day. Here is hoping that goes up and up and up, already better-than-expected just a few weeks ago.\par \par \uc2 My loser, Prince Harry and \uc2 Meghan Markle\uc2 . The two estranged royals are again dumping on the royal family from their mansion in California and their big \uc2 Netflix\uc2  deal. They`re worried about their privacy now. So here is some advice. If you want privacy, don`t do a big interview with Oprah. It tends to get noticed.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: It does. Mollie, quickly, your winner and loser?\par \par \uc2 HEMINGWAY: My winners are Republican Governors Greg Abbott and \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 . When you look at who`s leading the Republican Party, it`s not anyone in Washington, D.C. It`s these governors who are not just opening up their states, stopping their unconstitutional mandates, but also taking on big tech companies as both of these governors are, these big tech companies that are censoring conservatives.\par \par \uc2 My loser of the week is the National Guard, and it`s not the National Guard really, but the people who are using and exploiting the National Guard for political ends. We`re told that they need to stay in occupation of D.C. in perpetuity for these mysterious threats that never seem to be realized. It`s a shame and they need to be sent back home.\par \par \uc2 As long as they are here, we need to treat them better.\par \par \uc2 Up next, "Notable Quotables."\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 BREAM: Finally, tonight, "Notable Quotables."\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2 , FORMER PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: A Republican president will make a triumphant return to the White House. And I wonder who that will be.\par \par \uc2 SEN. CHUCK SCHUMER (D-NY): This bill is not a liberal wish list. This is an American wish list.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: It`s chockfull of spending porn. That is what I call it.\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: The last thing we need is neanderthal thinking that in the meantime everything is fine, take off your mask.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: The Biden administration was releasing illegal immigrants into our communities who had COVID. That is a neanderthal type approach.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: I think there is a challenge at the border that we are managing.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Not knowing who is walking around on your land, how many, and where they are headed. It`s just not very comforting.\par \par \uc2 GOV. ANDREW CUOMO\uc2  (D-NY): I now understand that I acted in a way that made people feel uncomfortable.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: I understood him loud and clear. It just didn`t go the way he planned.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: They canceled Mr. Potato Head. They canceled "The Muppets." They are canceling Dr. Seuss from the reading programs.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Do you guys remember Dixie Chicks?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: I hated them. They are terrible.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Dixie Chicks had their CDs trampled on their concerts cancelled.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Vaccine, vaccine, vaccine. Don`t be such a chicken squat. Get out there and get your shot.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BREAM: This weekend on FOX NEWS SUNDAY, Chris Wallace will speak with Arkansas Republican Governor \uc2