h's Capitol riot is moving at an unprecedented speed. Acting Deputy Attorney General John Carlin says the Justice Department has charged more than 300 individuals and arrested more than 280 so far.\par \par \uc2 One of those is Richard Michetti of Ridley Park in suburban Philadelphia. He was discovered after his former girlfriend called the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , and said he had called her and bragged about attending the uprising.\par \par \uc2 The district attorney in Los Angeles County is under fire tonight over his hiring of a public defender who has called L.A. police officers barbarians and is an advocate for the abolition of prisons.\par \par \uc2 Chief correspondent Jonathan Hunt has the story.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN HUNT, FOX NEWS CHIEF CORRESPONDENT (voice-over): Los Angeles County district attorney George Gascon campaigned on the idea that he would revolutionize the way crime and punishment is handled in L.A. and now he is following through.\par \par \uc2 But the D.A. is getting pushback from many prosecutors. The latest outcry is over Tiffiny Blacknell, a former public defender who campaigned on Gascon's behalf, now pointed to a high-ranking prosecutor role, a position in which she will need to work with the \uc2 Los Angeles Police Department\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 That might be difficult given a tweet from last June when L.A. was rocked by sometimes violent protests in the wake of the death of \uc2 George Floyd\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Responding to pictures of police using batons, Blacknell wrote, "Look at these barbarians. LAPD is an occupying army. Defund police."\par \par \uc2 She also posted a selfie wearing a t-shirt that read, the police are trained to kill us. And while her job would routinely involve obtaining prison sentences for certain criminals, Blacknell has also tweeted that "Prison is obsolete."\par \par \uc2 All of which has left some in the D.A.s office wandering what Gascon is thinking.\par \par \uc2 CINDY WALLACE, DEPUTY DISTRICT ATTORNEY, LOS ANGELES COUNTY: He says that he wants to work with us, he wants to make L.A. County a safer and better place, but he is bringing in people who do not believe in law enforcement and do not believe in prosecuting crime --\par \par \uc2 HUNT: In a statement to Fox News, the D.A.'s office said, "D.A. Gascon has the utmost confidence in his executive team and is looking forward to having Tiffiny Blacknell joined the office.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HUNT: Gascon is being sued by some of his D.A.s over the reforms, but he says they were in the campaign platform, and he, therefore, has a mandate to carry them out. Bret.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Jonathan Hunt in L.A. Jonathan, thanks.\par \par \uc2 Up next, what is vaccine hunting and how does one do it? Is it right for you or your family? We'll explain.\par \par \uc2 First, here is what some of our Fox affiliates around the country are covering tonight. Fox 11 in Los Angeles says a huge fire burned stacks of pallets and buses in the commercial area of the county. The inferno erupted in Compton before dawn and created a massive column of smoke that rose high into the sky, spread widely across the metropolitan area.\par \par \uc2 Fox 5 in New York, where the attorney general is reviewing a letter from state senators requesting an investigation into sexual harassment allegations against Democratic Governor \uc2 Andrew Cuomo\uc2 . Former aide has accused Cuomo of kissing her and making crude comments. Cuomo's office has denied those allegations.\par \par \uc2 And this is a live look at St. Louis from our affiliate Fox 2 there. One of the big stories there tonight. A report that Rush Limbaugh was laid to rest during a private ceremony Wednesday. That's according to the Southeast Missourian newspaper. A local radio station reports the funeral was private, was attended by about 40 people. Limbaugh's widow says there will be a virtual ceremony at a later date.\par \par \uc2 That's tonight's live look "OUTSIDE THE BELTWAY" from SPECIAL REPORT, we'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: \uc2 The U.S. Food and Drug Administration\uc2  Advisory Committee has endorsed the single-dose coronavirus vaccine by drug maker \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2 . The \uc2 FDA\uc2  is expected to quickly follow that recommendation and make that shot the third vaccine authorized for emergency use in the U.S., and that's a one-time dose.\par \par \uc2 The Navy says two U.S. warships in the Persian Gulf have suffered coronavirus outbreaks. The fifth fleet says the ships will likely be out of action for a few days. It says about a dozen crewmembers aboard the USS San Diego have tested positive. And the USS Philippine Sea also has several people who may be infected.\par \par \uc2 One of the president's top coronavirus advisers says nearly half of all Americans over the age of 65 have now received their first vaccine shot. Tonight, correspondent Casey Stegall looks at a new phenomena called vaccine hunting.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO TAPE)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: One, two, and three.\par \par \uc2 CASEY STEGALL, FOX NEWS CORRESPONDENT: As millions of Americans roll up their sleeves to receive a COVID vaccine, millions more wait their turn.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: The appointments are so hard to get.\par \par \uc2 STEGALL: Jose (ph) Espinosa (ph) and Cynthia (ph) Perez (ph) live in California but are part of a growing movement across the country known as vaccine hunting.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: I am here in hopes that there is any that might be left over.\par \par \uc2 STEGALL: These vaccine chasers show up at distribution sites before they close in the event other people don't make their appointments. Location managers say that can lead to extras, because each vial contains 10 doses, and once opened cannot be restored for the next day, so they would go to waste.\par \par \uc2 WILL BAKER, CARE AMBULANCE CLINIC MANAGER: We need to make sure that if they 