ationship to the Hastings law firm.\par \par \uc2 Meantime, FOX News has already reported the Lincoln Project paid $27 million to a consulting firm run by Lincoln Project cofounder Reed Galen. Now CNBC is reporting that Galen also ran a dark money group called Project Yellowstone, which was directly connected to the Lincoln Project. It's not illegal, but could have led to even more money going Galen's way. Laura?\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Trace, thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 And moments ago, Joe Biden managed to smear our men and women in uniform as, well, white supremacists.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: I worry about ongoing threats to our country from Americans who embrace white supremacy and conspiracies that align with it. What can your administration do to address this complex and wide-ranging problem?\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN, (D) PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: It's complex, it's wide- ranging, and it's real. And I would make sure we in fact focus on how to deal with the rise of white supremacy, and the studies that are beginning to be done about the impact of former military, former police officers, on the growth of white supremacy.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Joining me now is Chris Bedford, senior editor at "The Federalist." Chris, this was a meandering, kind of at times hard to follow series of answers from Biden, but that comment was just plain insulting and infuriating to police officers that I saw commenting just now online.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS BEDFORD, SENIOR EDITOR, "THE FEDERALIST": We just saw that coming out, and we've seen that coming out before probably about 10 years ago when there were concerns about people who were coming back from Afghanistan and Iraq and getting in American theaters and trying to make sure that they got the proper mental health protections that they needed. That somehow turned into fear that they would be dangerous, that they would be shooters, that they would 