omers' ability from buying more stock and selling stocks. Many everyday investors now are vowing to hold the line and keep sending the message to these hedge funds of Wall Street and those they see is trying to rig the system.\par \par \uc2 And coming up, we will have a lot of reaction. We'll get analysis, Lou Dobbs, Dan Bongino tonight.\par \par \uc2 But first, it's after 9:00 p.m. and our nation's capital, and that probably means that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is likely fast asleep. It's been an exhausting few days for Joe. He signed a record 40 executive orders and actions into, quote, "law" after just nine days in office. In other words, he has tripled the amount of executive orders signed by Trump, Obama, and Bush combined at this point in their presidencies.\par \par \uc2 Now, instead of the unity that was promised, Joe is literally acting unilaterally to enact every aspect of his radical socialist agenda, and he is doing it all with the stroke of a pen and its consequences are severe. It is so bad, even "The \uc2 New York Times\uc2 " editorial board ever so gently and ever so politely encouraged Biden to ease up on the executive orders, and at least try to acknowledge there are three branches of government. You are the executive branch. Then we have this other branch, the legislative branch.\par \par \uc2 And even this ever-so-mild criticism of Biden, it caused many on the radical left, they became unglued completely unhinged. How dare "The \uc2 New York Times\uc2 " do that! You get scores of these blue check mark liberals on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  lashing out at "The \uc2 New York Times\uc2 ". One frequent MSDNC guest calling them cowardly, another left-wing activist calling them moronic. By the way, when Democrats are busy fighting each other, just let the flight go on.\par \par \uc2 How dare "The Times" write anything other than glowing praise for the dear comrades and weak leader?\par \par \uc2 And, of course, this op-ed does pale greatly in comparison to how they covered \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and other conservatives in his first few weeks of office. One headline reads, "Mr. Trump's threat to Europe's security". Another quote, "President Trump's reckless shame game."\par \par \uc2 Seven months into his term, "The Times" ran an article entitled "The failing Trump presidency." Wow, that was quick.\par \par \uc2 And sadly, this is about so much more of the media bias, because with the stroke of a pen, that's it, a pen, Biden's litany of executive orders are causing real, serious, life-changing problems for tens of thousands of hardworking men and women, our fellow Americans, right here and right now, they are suffering. Thousands already receiving their pink slips after Joe canceled the Keystone XL pipeline. Stop border wall construction, up to 58,000 more could soon be unemployed because of this new ban on drilling on federal lands, a lot more to follow.\par \par \uc2 These are high-paying, yes, blue-collar, high skill jobs, gone, not easily, if at all, replaceable, all with the stroke of the frail, weak, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's hand. A pen in his hand.\par \par \uc2 Socialist Congresswoman Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez, she thinks this is great! What a great day! I'm not making it up.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REP. ALEXANDRIA OCASIO-CORTEZ (D-NY): Now, I'm feeling extraordinarily encouraged, and I think that the significance of President Biden's executive orders communicate a lot. One is that it really communicates that he meant what he said on the campaign trail, that he would make climate change a central priority of his administration and that he considers that not just a national security threat, but frankly, a global matter that it is. But it also really -- it also really signifies a good-faith openness and relationship to those activist communities.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Congresswoman, with all due respect, your Green New Deal policies, you're bragging about Joe's enacting, they resulted in great American workers, your fellow Americans, getting fired. Tell me, where are they going to work next week? And how are they going to pay their bills? How are they going to put food on their table, or pay their rent, or make mortgage payments, or car or truck payments? How are they going to pay for health care, or insurance, or day-to-day living? Do you even care?\par \par \uc2 Because I see zero compassion from you and \uc2 John Kerry\uc2  and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2 , and let's see, Granholm and the rest of you. Hardworking, law-abiding, taxpaying men and women, working men and women out of work, with all of the promises -- we want you to get new union jobs.\par \par \uc2 Well, the high-paying jobs that disappear, for example, and Congresswoman Ocasio-Cortez's own districts, remember, she ran \uc2 Amazon\uc2  right out of her district. The world is ending, and the New Green Deal is far more important. She says the world is ending -- than tens of thousands of American jobs.\par \par \uc2 The onward march for socialism must be our top priority. Maybe Congresswoman Ocasio-Cortez actually thinks that she is saving the planet. And by the way, one out of work American at a time, right? And, of course, in reality, this Green New Deal socialist agenda is hurting our fellow Americans. It's hurting the country.\par \par \uc2 And by the way, it will hurt the planet. Let me tell you how. The world is still, whether you like it or not, reliant, the lifeblood of the world's economy is energy, oil, gas, coal, and guess what? People will still be buying it, Americans will still be using it, and guess what? We will have to now get more of it from, well, in a lot of countries that we view as hostile regimes -- you know, Russia, Iran, China, countries in the Middle East that hate our guts, those would be countries that don't really give a rip about the environment, either.\par \par \uc2 In other words, hostile regimes run by hostile actors around the world, they are going to get rich and powerful. They are doing back flips. They want to send you "thank you" cards.\par \par \uc2 And pollution will likely also get worse. This doesn't seem to matter to anybody in the Biden administration, anyone supporting this madness. For example, Biden special climate envoy, \uc2 John Kerry\uc2 , he has long flown all over the world. He owns his big private own jet, causing, by the way, his own massive carbon footprint.\par \par \uc2 Now, Congresswoman Ocasio-Cortez, perhaps you should ask your fellow climate change supporter, \uc2 John Kerry\uc2 , who has no problems telling people you are out of work, this is more important, may be that jet pollutes more in a given year than most Americans will in their entire lives!\par \par \uc2 Now, I think maybe you should ask \uc2 John Kerry\uc2  if he cares about the client (ph), why doesn't he lead by example? How about he orders that his private jet be grounded, and in fairness, don't sell it, because it would still be a carbon footprint, he should have it disassembled, so it can never be used again, then you can recycle all the materials.\par \par \uc2 And while we are at it, all of Biden cabinet officials, they should stop using the private jets, and you might not know this, but you, the American taxpayer, pay for it. You foot the bill for what is a fleet, a massive fleet of private jets and aircraft used by federal officials and cabinet members.\par \par \uc2 Now, think about it. If we are currently facing this great climate crisis and Congresswoman Ocasio-Cortez's right, we only have 12 years, and it's that serious, that oil and gas workers are going to lose their high-paying career jobs and lose their health care and maybe lose their homes, not be able to save for their futures, send their kids to college, then shouldn't Biden officials lead by example, stop flying on the private jets that we, the American taxpayers, are paying for?\par \par \uc2 Now, I'm waiting for Congresswoman Ocasio-Cortez, \uc2 John Kerry\uc2 , \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2 , \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , \uc2 Jennifer Granholm\uc2 , I'm waiting for their answer. I want Joe to issue an executive order grounding the entire government fleet that we, the taxpayers, are paying for. This kind of heartless hypocrisy is disgusting. If you want to be leaders, and by example.\par \par \uc2 They don't care about we, the hardworking men and women in this country. More specifically, those that lost, again, good paying, well skilled, career jobs. Let them work elsewhere, \uc2 John Kerry\uc2  exclaimed, you know, saying. It's a worthy sacrifice. A worthy sacrifice, according to \uc2 Jennifer Granholm\uc2 , where is her sacrifice?\par \par \uc2 And just go out and find another union job, says the ever really experienced Mayor Pete. Mayor of South Bend.\par \par \uc2 The party who claims to have a monopoly on compassion for all of us, I'm not seeing much compassion at all for all these hardworking Americans that are anxious and can sleep tonight, and worried where the next paycheck is going to come from, and wondering whether or not it will ever be able to replace the good jobs you just took from them. And remember, these job killing policies didn't go through Congress, stroke of a pen, thousands and thousands unemployed, because \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , listening to the radical left that controls him.\par \par \uc2 He did it with a stroke of a pen. A few months ago on the campaign trail, there was Biden, he was claiming that governing by executive fiat was something that dictators do. No, we've got to get the votes, he said. That is -- this is a democracy.\par \par \uc2 What happened, Joe? In case you forgot, which is likely, I will remind you.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: I've got to get the votes. I've got to get the votes. That's why, you know, the one thing -- I have this strange notion, we are a democracy. Some of my Republican friends and some of my Democratic friends even occasionally say, well, if you can't get the votes, by executive order, you're going to do something. Things you can't do by executive order, unless you're a dictator. We are a democracy, and we need consensus.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: More than three times the number of executive orders in all three of his previous presidents. Biden's press secretary apparently trying to rewrite history. Let's take a look at this lie.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REPORTER: Does it suggest that President Biden sees himself as perhaps a benevolent dictator?\par \par \uc2 JEN PSAKI\uc2 , WHITE HOUSE PRESS SECRETARY: Well, Rob, I'm sure this was not your intention, but I think you took the president's comments a bit out of context. He was asked about tax reform and whether that could be done via executive order during the interview with George Stephanopoulos, what you're referring to.\par \par \uc2 REPORTER: (INAUDIBLE) question, but I think --\par \par \uc2 PSAKI: Well, I think -- I think the question is pretty important context for everybody, and he said no. And the president also said during an columnists back in December, that he didn't think executive action should be used for everything, and that certainly is his point of view.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Three times the executive orders in the same time frame that Bush 43, Obama, and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , I thought you promised you weren't going to lie to the American people. That would be, yeah, the fact-check lie list. And, of course, Biden's 40 and counting executive orders don't exactly spell unity, do they?\par \par \uc2 And, just today, he signed off on an order banning, get this, top priority, the term "China virus" in his White House, or "Wuhan virus" from being used at any federal level. I don't know why. Even though China and Wuhan, we are talking about geographical locations.\par \par \uc2 You know, even though China, hate to say it, Joe, they were responsible for the virus. Remember, they put the travel ban in effect, couldn't travel out of Wuhan to the rest of China, couldn't travel from the rest of China to Wuhan, but you could travel from Wuhan anywhere in the world.\par \par \uc2 And, by the way, where is the order banning the term, I guess, "German measles" is next, or "the new COVID, South African variant of COVID-19."\par \par \uc2 But, hey, when you rule by executive fiat, I guess facts don't matter. Debate certainly doesn't matter. And apparently neither do American workers. They're the people that wake up every day.\par \par \uc2 They work hard. They play by the rules. They obey the laws. They pay their taxes. They raise their kids. They put in -- they wake up, shovel coffee down their throat, make kids lunch for school, they raced off to works, do the 12-14 hours come help their kids with homework, they feed them, they put them to bed, they literally pass out exhausted every day.\par \par \uc2 Well, they want to have that luxury anymore if this continues. Tens of thousands will be losing their job.\par \par \uc2 Joining us now, three of those Americans directly impacted by Joe's climate crackdown, business manager of Pipeliners Union, 798, Danny Hendrix, is with us.\par \par \uc2 Danny, thank you for being with us.\par \par \uc2 Welding foreman and member of the Pipeliners Union 798, Billy Burns.\par \par \uc2 And the president of the Western Energy Alliance, Kathleen Sgamma is with us.\par \par \uc2 Thank you all for being with us.\par \par \uc2 Danny, let me start with you.\par \par \uc2 All right. You have 87 of your members laid off the day that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  signed the order. Now, I don't want to get nosy, but it takes a long time to be a professional pipeliner, right?\par \par \uc2 DANNY HENDRIX, BUSINESS MANAGER OF PIPELINERS UNION 798: That's correct.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You spent how many years in the business?\par \par \uc2 HENDRIX: I've been in 42 years.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Okay, I don't want to get too nosy, but can you give me a range of what people are making that have been doing this with the kind of experience that you and the guys laid off have?\par \par \uc2 HENDRIX: Well, on a good year, a welder can make $250,000 to 300,000.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: $250,000 or $350,000, did I hear you right?\par \par \uc2 HENDRIX: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Danny, is that job going to be easily replaceable? I would imagine this is a very specific skill for this very specific industry, am I right about that?\par \par \uc2 HENDRIX: Well, there is more certified heart doctors than there are certified pipeline welders. I mean, this is a highly trained craft.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Okay, now, you heard \uc2 John Kerry\uc2 , \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2 , you watched \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . How do you feel? How do your 87 fellow members laid off on the day you sign the order feel now?\par \par \uc2 HENDRIX: Well, you know, I feel for those 87 members, and a lot of them I know personally, and -- but what I really worry about is the next step, where you put the moratoriums on permits, the new work coming in, where your drilling or exploring more permitting for new wells, because the big picture -- I think a lot of people are missing, the big picture is, if you wanted to have a playbook to wipe out a nation, you take away their energy, or you take away their supply chain, and this is a perfect way to do it.\par \par \uc2 As you start with the pipelines, and then you go to the oil wells, then -- it's ludicrous that we are going to try to kill our own industry for our enemies.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well, that's exactly what is going to end up happening, because I don't think those windmills and solar panels are going to be online anytime soon, and we will be importing oil once again. By the way, please send my prayers to all your guys, saying we care about them, okay? I hope