--\par \par \uc2 BURNS: Twenty-five dollars an hour, and these guys, they make upwards to $250,000 a year.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Wow, and a good year, amazing.\par \par \uc2 And even somebody starting out --\par \par \uc2 BURNS: It's a good profit.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 Kathleen, let's talk about your group, \uc2 Western Energy\uc2 . I know that your group put together, you actually believe and have calculated, tell me how you got this number, the gross domestic product across eight Western states is going to go down $33.5 billion, that nearly 59,000 jobs are going to be cut annually, wages will drop $15 billion, with a b, state tax revenue will plummet $8.3 billion.\par \par \uc2 You know, probably government, liberal, socialist, New Green Dealers will say, that's not true, they are making that up.\par \par \uc2 Tell us how you got to your numbers.\par \par \uc2 KATHLEEN SGAMMA, PRESIDENT OF WESTERN ENERGY ALLIANCE: It's not my number, it's the number from a University of Wyoming professor who looked at the exact scenario that President Biden did yesterday. With the stroke of a pen, he said no more leasing on federal lands, and in the West, where development of oil and natural gas happens on federal land, eight states, where 97 percent of that production takes place, would lose those 58,000 jobs, the $33.5 billion in GDP, and on. You know, it would blow a hole in the Wyoming and New Mexico state budgets.\par \par \uc2 So it puts at risk not just the workers but services -- needed services, education, public health. It puts those states at risk for providing those services as well. And that's why we sued as soon as he signed the order.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah, and I've got to imagine there's a lot of anxiety and uncertainty for all of the people that are involved here.\par \par \uc2 Danny, you're talking to your guys. Your guys laid off on day one, the day this thing was signed. What are they -- I assume many of them own homes, many of them