2 We are praying for you guys. I wish I had answers, and I wish I could help, and I know a lot of other Americans feel the same way, with these families, and you families are facing, should not happen, stroke of a pen, goodbye, career job. It's unbelievable. The callousness is unreal.\par \par \uc2 Thank you all for what you do. We are praying for y'all that y'all get up and running fast. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 HENDRIX: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Coming up, a classic example, David versus Goliath. David was winning. The government jumped on Goliath side. We will explain and give you the real scoop on \uc2 GameStop\uc2  and Robinhood, and by the way, you are not going to believe which Biden cabinet member was paid a fortune by a hedge fund at the center of it all.\par \par \uc2 Lou Dobbs and Dan Bongino, straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And tonight, we continue to follow the ongoing David versus Goliath brawl that has broken out on Wall Street. Tonight, as a group of small -- small-time, main street traders taking on the big headphones goliath's who got caught in a massive, what they do is they short stocks in a short squeeze, they lost billions after retail investors, they banded together to buy stocks like \uc2 GameStop\uc2 , AMC, \uc2 BlackBerry\uc2 , and others.\par \par \uc2 Now, how is the establishment responding to getting beaten by the little guy? Well, they have been freezing trades on apps like Robinhood and even censoring online message boards, and get this, we are now learning tonight, Treasury Secretary \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2 , right there, she was paid a whopping $800,000 from the hedge fund Citadel, which is one of the funds at the center of this controversy.\par \par \uc2 Now, ask yourself, hire a speaker for an event you have, let me see, who could I hire, oh, \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2 , we'll give her $800,000. We have to face a simple truth here. There is, there always has been, too many financial Wall Street and political ties with Wall Street and people in government. I'm not saying anything nefarious, I'm saying, hmm, I wonder if they hired her for great knowledge and interesting speaking style.\par \par \uc2 Biden White House downplaying the payments and the entire \uc2 GameStop\uc2  story, but it is already now drawing bipartisan calls for investigations on Capitol Hill. Somebody who knows a lot more about this than me, the author of "The Trump Century". He's the host of the number one show on our sister network, "Lou Dobbs Tonight", the one and only, Lou Dobbs.\par \par \uc2 You know, I think Jeanine and your monologues scare me more than my own monologues. I don't know. Good to see you, Lou.\par \par \uc2 LOU DOBBS, \uc2 FOX BUSINESS NETWORK\uc2  HOST: Great to see you, Sean.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Can we break this down? Hedge funds, shorting stocks, it's part of a process, little guys banding together, now looks like -- and then they stopped, people can't cash out at this point, things got ugly today.\par \par \uc2 DOBBS: The word "rigged" we heard a lot under the previous president, didn't we? This is a rigged event. And that is Robinhood, which has all sorts of rigged positive wonderful connotations, it's CEO today deciding to disrupt the market, and particularly to the disadvantage of those who were buying stock in a company that big money had said would only decline.\par \par \uc2 But this is a complicated story. More complicated than it's being presented, because there are a lot of hedge funds on the other side of these trades standing with those folks who started this acquisition effort, buying up the stock as the shorts primarily from the hedge funds moved in. But there's also those hedge funds on the long side of this, Sean. So it gets complicated.\par \par \uc2 The actions taken by Robinhood and several other internet brokerages today to change the rules of Wall Street right in the middle of this event probably means that Robinhood will 