LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 BRET BAIER, FOX NEWS ANCHOR: Home tonight. That's it for this Special Report. Fair, balanced and still unafraid. It's been a busy week; we've got one more day before the weekend. The Story hosted by Martha MacCallum starts right now. Hey, Martha.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA MACCALLUM, FOX NEWS ANCHOR: Good to see you, Bret. Thank you. So good evening, everybody. I'm Martha MacCallum in New York, and this is The Story tonight. So, Americans vote every four years and they've got a choice of who leads for the following for, the loser goes home, unchosen by the voters and that's how our representative democracy works. And the people who supported that losing candidate, they go on with their lives hoping that next time their candidate will prevail.\par \par \uc2 But this time, the winning side seems to want to burn down everything touched by the outgoing president. Anyone who even served in his administration in any way, anyone who went to the Ellipse or any rally for that matter, and maybe even anybody who buys MAGA hats online arouses some suspicion. And certainly, anyone who had the audacity to vote for him.\par \par \uc2 Think about this for comparison. \uc2 Richard Nixon\uc2  was about to be convicted by the Senate for criminal conduct when he resigned and left Washington. He was vilified in that era. But by contrast, he and his supporters look like they got off easy. This treatment that we are seeing now is unprecedented in American history, perhaps most similar to the blacklists of McCarthyism, which swept up many people who just had innocuous associations and no dream of supplanting their government with communism. Now, watch this from last night as Don Lemon talks about the Americans who dared to vote for President Trump.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DON LEMON, CNN HOST: If you voted for Trump, you voted for the person who the Klan supported. You voted for the person who Nazis support. You voted for the person who the right supports. That's the crowd that you are in. You voted for the person who incited a crowd to go into the Capitol and potentially take the lives of lawmakers, took the lives of police officers, took the lives of - innocent lives who were there on the Capitol that day. You voted on that side.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: 74 million Americans out of a total of 328 million, essentially being called racists and bigots. That's a lot of Americans and many of you.\par \par \uc2 Let's bring in House Minority Whip Steve Scalise, who objected to the Electoral College results and voted against the latest impeachment. Good to see you this evening, Congressman Scalise. Thanks for being here. What goes through your mind when you listen to that?\par \par \uc2 REP. STEVE SCALISE (R-LA): Good to be with you, Martha. Well, Martha, the disappointing thing there is that that is the playbook of the cancer culture socialist left. They don't want to talk about issues. They want to just demonize the opposition because their ideas are very radical. I mean, the things they talk about taking away people's rights, the Green New Deal, raising taxes, all the things that they really stand for, they don't want to talk about publicly. So, they just want to demonize the opposition, cancel you on social media. Those are the things that that are the classic tactics of the cancel culture. I think people are fed up with that. Let's focus on actual things that matter to families, not trying to demonize someone who disagrees with you on issues.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: So, for all of the discussion about, you know, it was going to be 20 members of the House that were going to vote for impeachment, there was this sort of feeling that this sentiment was sweeping on both sides, that \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  was open to this idea of impeachment.\par \par \uc2 In the end, the numbers looked basically like they looked last time around, 10 members of the GOP ended up voting for this and two-thirds voted to question the results of the election. And obviously that has had some backlash. But my question for you is, where is the Republican Party at this point? Is it the party of Trump, because we're looking at these numbers that show, given everything that's happened, still tremendous support for President Trump? And I want you to listen to what some of these folks said at that event who were outside of it. Watch this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Will you ever support any of the Republicans who are not standing up for the president right now?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: No, no, absolutely not.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: This is a Trump Party. Those guys are done.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: It's a new party. The Republican Party, in my opinion, is dead.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: 2022 is going to be a brutal year for you. And every race for dogcatcher, for state legislature, for any judge is going to be a bloodbath for the establishment of Republican.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Do you think that's true?\par \par \uc2 SCALISE: Well, Martha, clearly the president has tremendous support over the last four years in the things that he's done. You look at where the country is right now, it's a divided country already. And it was like that before the election. But there are millions of people who are disgusted by what they saw, like I was last week in the Capitol, the anarchists that broke in the capital, those millions of people that were disgusted by that also are passionate conservatives who love this country and love the conservative who love this country and love the conservative values that make our country great.\par \par \uc2 And frankly, the policies that the president carried through the last four years to rebuild our economy, to rebuild our military, to stand up to ISIS