was giving in a sense, the liberals, the Left, the establishment, a warning you're going too far and it will actually harm and not help your interests over time. And of course he gets punished for having made that very sensible piece.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: No, of course. Well, former Republican Senator and Never Trumper himself, Bob Corker let a little bit of the truth slip today.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BOB CORKER, FORMER TENNESSEE SENATOR: I'm actually glad I hate what happened - what has happened in our country. But I'm actually thankful that people have been able to see the president's true character. Never allow this type of person ever to become the Republican nominee and certainly be president of the United States.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Glad - I mean, I said this to one of my producers the other day. I said, I hate to say this, but it seems like the Left, some of the people on MSNBC seem to be - I don't think they want people hurt, but they're enjoying this moment because then they can say, "See, I told you so."\par \par \uc2 And then we find out of course, that one of the guys at the riot, John Sullivan - we'll get into that later, was anti-Trump, Antifa, anarchist, whatever you want to call them. Anarchist who was causing trouble long before this rally, and he obviously was not a supporter of the president to say the least,\par \par \uc2 ANTON: This is the culmination of an effort to destroy the president. Now - I mean, I'm certainly - let me just back up and say. I'm not saying he had no role in January 6th, and that he's completely blameless in all of this. But there's been an attempt over time to say, well, we finally got him now, whether it was this tape or Russia or whatever.\par \par \uc2 He's finally done this, he's finally done that. He'll be cut off from his supporters and everything. And so, they - January 6th gave them an opportunity to finally do something they've wanted to do for a long 