upposed to be the smartest guy who ever lived, so what's happening here?\par \par \uc2 REP. BOB GOOD (R-VA): This is an inexcusable impeachment proceeding that happened. It's a sham, as we all know. There was no basis for it and it's inexcusable for the third ranking leader of the Republican party to vote with the Democrats for this.\par \par \uc2 The conference chair is in charge of communications and messaging and to make herself into a talking point for the Democrats where they would beat us over the head over - during the course of the impeachment proceedings with her words were before her vote and for her to vote for impeachment is just inexcusable.\par \par \uc2 Leadership is a privilege. It comes with responsibility and that responsibility has been irreparably violated. To vote to impeach with just a week left in the president's term - seven days left, meaning it would have no impact, you're not removing him early. He's already leaving office in seven days from yesterday's vote.\par \par \uc2 To do that, it was not only wrong for President Trump, just to try to harm him, to damage him, to try to tarnish his legacy, but it's wrong for the Republican Party and it's wrong for the country most importantly.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, we found out - the \uc2 FBI\uc2  found out, they did the briefing that the planning for this converging on the Capitol took place in the days preceding Trump's speech. So the whole idea that the speech - it was happening while the speech was still going on, I believe. You correct me if I'm wrong, I'm pretty sure that's correct. And I'm not saying no mistakes were made--\par \par \uc2 GOOD: That's correct.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: But come on. But I got to ask you this question about Liz Cheney. I have nothing against her personally. I'm sure she's a wonderful person - I really don't. But if you're going to be one of the key leaders of the Republican Party, shouldn't you agree with the Republican voters on key issues? Not be in opposition to your own base, like playing against your own base?\par \par \uc2 GOOD: Yes, what does this say? This is perhaps the most important vote any of us will ever take to remove a president or at least to symbolically do that, because there's only a week left in his term. But to do that when the chips are down, the most important vote.\par \par \uc2 And this is a president who has given us record low unemployment, the greatest economy of our lifetime, more strong border control, peace in the Middle East, what he's done on energy independence, conservative judges of Supreme Court, to try to tarnish that legacy because you have a personal vindication against him, personal revenge to try to tarnish his legacy, just inexcusable. And that's why myself and others are calling for her to step down as a leader of the Republican Party.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, Congressman a Left-Wing activist I referenced with Michael Anton, has now been charged in the Capitol riot. He says he was just there to document what's going on, except Fox News is reporting that Sullivan can allegedly be heard egging on the protesters in the video he provided to the \uc2 FBI\uc2 . Well, I read the \uc2 FBI\uc2 's affidavit.\par \par \uc2 And inside the building he told reporters that we got to get this "S" burned and it's our House. In fact, he was then caught on tape saying similar things during a DC riot over the summer.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOHN SULLIVAN, WASHINGTON DC, RIOTER: We (bleep) about to burn this (bleep) down. (bleep) this (bleep). We got to (bleep) rip Trump out of that office right over there. (bleep) pull him out of that (bleep). Nah, nah we ain't about (bleep) waiting until the next election we about to go get that (bleep).\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: But, I guess, we weren't doing like facial recognition and arresting him back then or were they or questioning him, maybe they were. But, I mean, we were we were raising this issue the other night last week that some of these people, they didn't appear to be the regular Trump rally people.\par \par \uc2 They seem to be tactically set up and some of them, I think, we're cueing on. But that guy obviously was just a Left-Wing activist telling people to keep it going. He said at one point you guys are savage, like breaking into the Capitol, like egging them on.\par \par \uc2 GOOD: Yes. Well, hopefully, justice will prevail. In the days ahead we'll learn what really happened and it'll be investigated and we want justice to prevail and folks to be prosecuted accordingly to whatever they're guilty of.\par \par \uc2 But to rush to judgment, to try to conflate together that the president is responsible when he said to go there peacefully or to say, because we're standing up for election integrity, that somehow that's the same thing as condoning the violence.\par \par \uc2 Republicans have stood with law enforcement and against violence always going back in all of our history and certainly over the past year while our cities were being burned and our police were being attacked and there was rioting and looting going on the Left.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes. Well, congressman you got to take your state a Commonwealth of Virginia back too, that's in a mess as well with Northam. So congressman thank you so much for joining us.\par \par \uc2 GOOD: Indeed it is.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And coming up, we're going to expose the frightening new ways that radical leftists are using the education system to indoctrinate kids and what it means to our future? Don't go away.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: A San Francisco Bay Area school is taking the brainwashing of our children to disturbing new heights. According to whistleblower documents obtained by my next guest, a third grade teacher at a Cupertino, California Elementary School forced students to deconstruct their identity and then rank themselves according to power and privilege.\par \par \uc2 The teacher also reportedly told students we live in a "dominant culture of white middle-class cisgender, educated, able-bodied, Christian English speaker - that's a mouthful, who created this culture in order to hold power and stay in power.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now is the man who uncovered that bigoted lesson Chris Rufo, Contributing Editor at City Journal. Chris, I'm guessing a concerned parent got you these documents, am I correct?\par \par \uc2 CHRIS RUFO, EDITOR, CITY JOURNAL: Yes. That's exactly right. A parent found out what was going on, was outraged. And in so many cases parents aren't able to do something, but in this case they brought the evidence of the principle and they demanded an end to it.\par \par \uc2 And I think that's really interesting is that this parent is actually Chinese American. This parent learned about the Cultural Revolution in China that started with this kind of demonization and struggle sessions, eventually leading to the deaths of millions. And she told me she's afraid that it's already happening here in the United States and these lessons terrified her to the core.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, I also think it's racist. I'm going to say it. I think they are racially dividing America at a time where our country is going through difficult times of the pandemic, our economy, obviously the upheaval politically. But I think it's racist. They're demonizing all people who are non-minority and throwing them all into some big pot of intolerance.\par \par \uc2 And then all these kids are like, what, I just want to go play kickball or --It's just bad. It's bad teaching, it's vindictive and it's propagandistic, so you're right. Chairman Mao would be thrilled.\par \par \uc2 Chris, one of the assignments given to the third graders in that school - I guess, it's a slide and it shows students were asked to write about their identities and how it impacts their privilege. This was all during a math class, is that right - math?\par \par \uc2 RUFO: Yes, it was during a math class and they asked students basically to deconstruct their identities - their racial identity, their sexual identity, whether they were transgender or not, and then create an identity map and decide which aspects of their identity were the oppressor and which aspects of their identity were the oppressed.\par \par \uc2 So they're not only dividing America along racial lines, but they're actually dividing eight and nine-year-old children along these lines that are generated first in academia in a kind of neo-Marxist theory, now being pushed at as low as elementary school level. And these kids have to be bewildered, but they trust their teachers, but unfortunately parents should do anything but trust these teachers. They have to find out what's going on and they have to stop it.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes. Well, if parents want their kids educated - really educated they certainly don't have time to engage in this nonsense. It looks like it's taken from an \uc2 Instagram\uc2  Live or \uc2 Facebook\uc2  Live of any random leftist on Capitol Hill. So Chris thank you for doing that. Thank you to the parent whoever you are for raising this issue.\par \par \uc2 So what's the ultimate goal here of this type of racial indoctrination that we just laid out? Well, an 18 year old Massachusetts girl used \uc2 twitter\uc2  to rat out her mom for attending the Capitol Hill protest last week.\par \par \uc2 "Hi mom, remember the time you told me I shouldn't go to BLM protest, because they could get violent. This is you?" She then showed a video purporting to show her mom after an altercation. We should note there's no indication her mother went into the Capitol Building, only that she was at the Trump march.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now is Carol Swain, former Princeton and Vanderbilt Professor. Carol what's going on here, turning child against parent?\par \par \uc2 CAROL SWAIN, FORMER VANDERBILT UNIVERSITY PROFESSOR: Well, it's the indoct