 when you could as easily wear three, or perhaps five masks?\par \par \uc2 DR. SCOTT JENSEN, MINNESOTA STATE SENATOR: Your exactly right, Laura. Actually, I did the math, and if you're going to have a five-micron core size, you probably should do 10 layers, and that would be good. But in the article, it speaks specifically that if you go more than two layers, then it might be hard to breathe. And this is exactly what parents have been saying, is let my child play without endangering his or her life. This is not science.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: You see, though, prominent people, I believe, was it Mitt Romney we saw, guys, wear a double mask. I think Biden even pushed two masks are better than one. We'll watch. Listen.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN, (D) PRESIDENT-ELECT: I walked in here with this mask, but I have one of the N95 masks underneath it. And I left in the dressing -- the room I was in before I got here. And so, I think it matters what we say.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: So, it matters what we say, a mask is not a political statement. California, what do they have 98 percent mask usage and they have the worst outbreak in the country, what's happening there. Maybe they need to double up, Dr. Jensen.\par \par \uc2 JENSEN: You're exactly right. If you actually look at mask compliance, it doesn't reflect a reduction in disease cases. And the study in Denmark was pretty clear. If you wore masks all the time or you didn't wear a mask at all, both situations averaged out to about two percent COVID-19 being contracted over a 30-day period.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I think the author of that study tried to back away, saying no one should think that masks aren't good, though. He kind of, I think got some blowback from that, so he stepped back. But anytime you mention the issue of masks, people just freak out and say you're an anti-masker or denier. But it is curious in states where we have such great mask compliance